Question: Determine whether the following two code snippets are semantic code clones.

Code 1: Python
```python
n = int(input())
total = 0
for i in range(1, n + 1):
    if i % 3 == 0 or i % 5 == 0:
        total += i
print(total)
```

Code 2: Java
```java
import java.util.*;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            if (i % 3 == 0 || i % 5 == 0) {
                total += i;
            }
        }
        System.out.println(total);
    }
}
```
<analysis>
Code 1 reads one integer n from standard input and prints the sum of the values in 1..n divisible by 3 or by 5.<end_of_step>

Code 2 reads one integer n from standard input and prints the same sum. Both sides are complete stdin-to-stdout programs.<end_of_step>

The loop bounds are easy to misread, so rather than predict Code 2's output, run both programs on the same input and compare what they actually print. Keep each step short so nothing is cut off.<end_of_step>
<end_of_analysis>

<code>
import subprocess
def run_both(s):
    py = subprocess.run(["python3", "candidate_code.py"], input=s, capture_output=True, text=True)
    jv = subprocess.run(["java", "-cp", ".", "Main"], input=s, capture_output=True, text=True)
    return py.stdout.strip(), jv.stdout.strip()

# Run both programs on the same inputs in this step and print both outputs.
for s in ["10", "100"]:
    out1, out2 = run_both(s)
    print(repr(s), "-> Code 1:", out1, "| Code 2:", out2)
