Question: Determine whether the following two code snippets are semantic code clones.

Code 1: Python
```python
a = int(input())
b = int(input())
print(a // b)
```

Code 2: Java
```java
import java.util.*;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        int b = sc.nextInt();
        System.out.println(a / b);
    }
}
```
<analysis>
Code 1 reads two integers from standard input and prints their quotient.<end_of_step>

Code 2 reads two integers from standard input and prints their quotient, but Java integer division truncates toward zero while Python's // floors.<end_of_step>

The two are textually near-identical, so this is a behavioural suspicion rather than a signature mismatch. That is exactly what running both sides settles, so test it instead of guessing. Keep each step short.<end_of_step>
<end_of_analysis>

<code>
